// 04-gross-margin-pct-function.tmdl
// Demo 4: reference answer for prompts/04-dax-udf.md. A DAX user-defined function and a measure that calls it.
//
// DAX user-defined functions: generally available since the June 2026 release of Power BI Desktop
// and the Power BI service. They need database compatibility level 1702 or higher
// (compatibilityLevel in definition/database.tmdl). Function names take letters, digits, underscores
// and dots (for namespaces); parameter names take no dots.


// ===== Option A: TMDL view in Power BI Desktop (a script, then Apply) =====

createOrReplace
	/// Gross margin as a share of revenue. Blank when revenue is zero or blank.
	function GrossMarginPct =
			(revenue : NUMERIC, cost : NUMERIC) =>
				DIVIDE ( revenue - cost, revenue )


// ===== Option B: the files of the Power BI Project, edited in VS Code =====

// definition/functions.tmdl  (one file for all the functions of the model)
// The file form is the script above without "createOrReplace", at the first level of indentation.
// To be confirmed in the lab: add the function once through TMDL view, export the PBIP and compare.

/// Gross margin as a share of revenue. Blank when revenue is zero or blank.
function GrossMarginPct =
		(revenue : NUMERIC, cost : NUMERIC) =>
			DIVIDE ( revenue - cost, revenue )


// definition/tables/salesInvoices.tmdl  (inside "table salesInvoices", after 'Gross Margin')

	/// Gross margin %, through the GrossMarginPct function.
	measure 'Gross Margin %' = GrossMarginPct ( [Revenue], [Cost] )
		formatString: 0.0%
